@@ -9,6 +9,33 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## WebMCP tools
+
+The app exposes tools through `document.modelContext` using Chrome's
+`use-webmcp-tool` React hook. The integration persists across Astro client-side
+navigation and does nothing in browsers without WebMCP. Use a WebMCP-enabled
+browser in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost).
+
+| Tool | Action |
+| --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | Search titles and summaries with `query` and optional `limit` (default 10, maximum 50). |
+| `get_reading_list` | Retrieve the current session's saved articles and links. |
+| `set_article_saved` | Set an article's saved state using `slug` and `saved`; repeated requests preserve the requested state. |
+| `open_article` | Navigate to a known article using its `slug`. |
+
+Find slugs with `search_articles`. Tools use the same session API as the UI;
+reading-list changes update mounted bookmarks and the reading-list flyout.
+Arguments are validated at execution time, network calls honor cancellation,
+and recoverable failures return an `error` field. Only known article slugs can
+be saved or opened. No cross-origin tool exposure is configured.
+
+Tool registration lives in `src/components/AgentTools.tsx`, definitions in
+`src/lib/news-tools.ts`, and shared client operations in `src/lib/news-client.ts`.
+See the [WebMCP imperative API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+
+Run automated tool checks with `pnpm test` (Node 22.18+), and build with
+`pnpm build`.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
